From: openEuler RISC-V Maintainers <noreply@example.invalid>
Date: Sun, 6 Sep 2026 00:00:00 +0000
Subject: [PATCH] cmake: resolve whole-archive link features

License: GPL-3.0-or-later
Upstream-Status: downstream-only
Origin: openEuler RISC-V packaging

CMake 3.27 rejects a link item that reaches an executable both through a
normal transitive link interface and through LINK_LIBRARY's WHOLE_ARCHIVE
feature.  The client, SDK bridge, and Rust archive deliberately use
WHOLE_ARCHIVE because they are mutually dependent, but tesseract_tk and
tesseract_client also propagate normal references to the same targets.

Override every occurrence of those three archives to WHOLE_ARCHIVE on the
two Linux Qt consumers.  This resolves the feature conflict without removing
an archive, changing symbol retention, or disabling the test executable.

Remove this patch when upstream applies an equivalent link-feature override
or otherwise removes the conflicting transitive default references.

---
 tests/CMakeLists.txt      | 3 +++
 ui/linux-qt/CMakeLists.txt | 3 +++
 2 files changed, 6 insertions(+)

diff --git a/tests/CMakeLists.txt b/tests/CMakeLists.txt
--- a/tests/CMakeLists.txt
+++ b/tests/CMakeLists.txt
@@ -379,6 +379,9 @@ else()
         tesseract_tk
     )
 endif()
+set_property(TARGET tesseract_tests PROPERTY LINK_LIBRARY_OVERRIDE
+    "WHOLE_ARCHIVE,tesseract_sdk_bridge_cxx,tesseract_client,tesseract_sdk_ffi-static")
+
 # Register each Catch2 TEST_CASE as an individual ctest test.
 include(Catch)
 # Keychain-touching tests share the OS credential store (libsecret /
diff --git a/ui/linux-qt/CMakeLists.txt b/ui/linux-qt/CMakeLists.txt
--- a/ui/linux-qt/CMakeLists.txt
+++ b/ui/linux-qt/CMakeLists.txt
@@ -129,6 +129,9 @@ target_link_libraries(tesseract_qt PRIVATE
     opus
 )
 
+set_property(TARGET tesseract_qt PROPERTY LINK_LIBRARY_OVERRIDE
+    "WHOLE_ARCHIVE,tesseract_sdk_bridge_cxx,tesseract_client,tesseract_sdk_ffi-static")
+
 if(WAYLAND_CLIENT_LIB AND Qt6GuiPrivate_FOUND)
     # The root project only enables LANGUAGES CXX. Enable C here so we can
     # compile the wayland-scanner generated .c protocol glue.
